docs {
  # Roll6 API
  
  Requests inherit Bearer auth from the collection; `User/Login` stores `token`.
  Create requests store ids (`mapModelId`, `campaignId`, `mapId`, `tokenId`, `mapTokenId`,
  `characterId`, `imageFileName`) as runtime variables used by the following requests.
  
  Running the whole collection in order (Runner) works end to end: each folder creates an
  extra record just to exercise its DELETE, so the records used by later folders survive.
  `User/Register` creates a new user with a random e-mail on every run.
  
  `Image/Upload` needs S3 (DigitalOcean Spaces) credentials configured on the API.
}
